  "full_text": "Now the soul of a Christian is to save people, right? So like, they might wear a white hat, right? Like, let's just say, that's what that reminds me of. And, or the good guy, right? He's the good guy. His soul is to save people. And it kind of almost pollutes his soul to like not do, to condemn people, right? Now the, a Jew is probably, they're supposed to, they wear a black hat. And their job is to condemn people. So two-thirds have to be saved. One-third has to be condemned. So the Christian's job is to save people. The Jew's job is to condemn people. And so, like, the military's job is to kill people. So it's possible that if you're in the military, declare yourself as a white hat or a black hat. You mark those that are saved, and then the black hat marks those that are condemned, and then you cross-check them, and you do round two, okay? So the black hat should only kill people. The white hat should only save people. And a person like me, I guess I'm wearing blue, like French or something. I don't know. The police, their job is to, well... They both condemn and save. So some people should only save people because it pollutes their soul to condemn them. Some people should only condemn people. And then there's the rest of them.",
